# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Ill-Timed Explosion draws two cards, then its optional two-card discard sets damage to the greatest discarded mana value.
# Forcing: The four lands can cast Explosion but not Lava Axe. Three damage clears the blocker and leaves the 2/4 attacker alive; five also kills that attacker.
# AI behavior: The opponent has no hand or mana and only a 3/3 blocker. The player chooses the discard and then attacks.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = Cancel and an Island were discarded, the blocker died, Those Who Serve survived, and its attack was lethal.
#   LOSE = the discard was declined and left the blocker, or too much damage killed the attacker.
#   TIMEOUT = the optional discard or two-card selection did not complete.
# Card roles:
#   Ill-Timed Explosion — draws cards and offers the variable-damage discard.
#   Cancel — the three-mana-value discard that sets useful damage.
#   Lava Axe — a five-mana-value trap that also kills the player's attacker.
#   Centaur Courser — the three-toughness blocker.
#   Those Who Serve — the four-toughness attacker that wins after the measured blast.
# Protocol path: Cast, draw two, discard two, resolve damage, then attack.
